  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional capacity assessment - Swisscontact</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kapacitetsstudie - Swisscontact</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser en kapacitetsstudie av organisationen Swisscontact, Guatemala. Ambassaden f&#xf6;rbereder finansiellt st&#xf6;d till Swisscontact och behov finns d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r att se &#xf6;ver Swisscontact&#x2019;s kapacitet att hantera och implementera insatsen, inklusive deras kapacitet f&#xf6;r intern styrning och kontroll, samt f&#xf6;r att bed&#xf6;ma deras kapacitet att uppn&#xe5; f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultat. Det finansiella st&#xf6;d som f&#xf6;rbereds, har diskuterats i ambassadens kommitt&#xe9; f&#xf6;r kvalitetss&#xe4;kring och en kapacitetsstudie av Swisscontact var en av kommitt&#xe9;ns rekommendationer. Detta &#xe4;r en st&#xf6;dinsats till huvudinsatsen som syftar till att bidra till urfolkskvinnors och ungdomars egenmakt.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution is an assessment of the institutional capacity of Swisscontact, Guatemala. The Embassy is preparing funding to Swisscontact and there is thus a need to assess the institutional capacity of Swisscontact to manage and implement the proposed project. The study will assess internal management and control, as well as the organisation&#x2019;s competence to deliver planned results and expected impacts. The proposed project has been discussed in the Embassy committee for quality assurance, and a capacity assessment of Swisscontact was one of the recommendations of the committee. This is a supporting contribution to the main contribution that aims to strengthen indigenous women and youth&apos;s economic empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
